// The Little Dot client row — ruled by JJ 2026-08-20: "having the logos on
// there can be a lil booster", tasteful, all the same off-white, and it
// must NEVER read as though he creative-directed for these brands. Round
// 6 adds Little Dot's own mark, and the guard got structural: the studio
// lives under "( at )" and the brands under the work-verbs label, so the
// employer can never be misread as a client and the brands can never be
// misread as creative direction.
//
// Marks are inline SVG, single fill, currentColor: below the flip this
// section is dark, so they render paper like everything else, and the
// colour rule (colour only inside the work) holds. The LDS mark is
// traced (potrace, 5x) from the 200px wordmark JJ supplied 2026-08-20 —
// swap in a cleaner vector from the brand kit whenever he brings one
// home, same slot. Pokemon is JJ's own pick (the outlined coloring-book
// mark he sent), traced the same way. The rest are public brand SVGs,
// monochromed; sources + the mono pipeline live in
// 06_Assets/agency-logos/ in the website Drive folder.
//
// STILL WANTED (JJ, 2026-08-20): the monster-trucks channel mark —
// which property, exactly, needs JJ to say; the row ships without it
// rather than guessing.
// --h is a per-mark optical size correction: these wordmarks have very
// different built-in heights, and one shared cap height reads uneven.
